{"results":[{"url":"https://www.indiatoday.in/fact-check/video/fact-check-video-did-pakistan-mps-chant-modi-modi-inside-parliament-1922816-2022-03-09","final_url":"https://www.indiatoday.in/fact-check/video/fact-check-video-did-pakistan-mps-chant-modi-modi-inside-parliament-1922816-2022-03-09","title":"Fact Check Video: Did Pakistan MPs chant ‘Modi, Modi’ inside Parliament?","description":"A video is being circulated on social media with the claim that it shows Pakistani MPs praising PM Modi for facilitating the evacuation of Pakistani students from Ukraine.","language":"en","text":"# Fact Check Video: Did Pakistan MPs chant 'Modi, Modi' inside Parliament?\n\nIndia Today Television\n\nNoida,UPDATED: Mar 9, 2022 21:22 IST\n\nA video is being circulated on social media with the claim that it shows Pakistani MPs praising PM Modi for facilitating the evacuation of Pakistani students from Ukraine. So, did Pakistan MPs chant ‘Modi, Modi’ inside Parliament? Watch this video to find out the truth.  \n  \n**MARCH 10: FOLLOW INDIA TODAY FOR ASSEMBLY ELECTION 2022 RESULTS**\n\nRead More\n\nMore videos from Fact Check\n\n### VIDEOS FROM OTHER SECTIONS\n\nIndia\n\nWorld\n\nNewsMo\n\nFact Check\n\nProgrammes\n\n### LATEST VIDEOS\n\n19:33\n\nThe Indian Air Force marked its 94th anniversary with a massive flypast over Varanasi's ghats, stretching from Namo Ghat to Assi Ghat in the presence of Prime Minister Narendra Modi. Featuring 94 aircraft across 31 formations, the grand finale involved fighter jets, transport planes, and helicopters drawn from 12 activated Air Force stations. Key aerial formations included the Prachand formation showcasing frontline combat aircraft with operational weapon loadouts, the Su-30MKI Hanuman formation, the Rafale Neelkanth formation executing a trishul breakout, and indigenous LCA Tejas aerial displays. Multi-service integration was highlighted through joint formations like Tridev and Nataraj involving the Indian Navy and Air Force assets. Addressing the occasion, IAF spokesperson Wing Commander Jaydeep Singh explained that the formations were given culturally resonant names inspired by Lord Shiva to connect with the heritage of Kashi, reflecting the synergy of faith and modern military capabilities.\n\n4:44\n\nActor Dhanush has reorganised his fan network into a welfare movement named Dhanush Narppani Iyakkam, sparking speculation about a potential political foray in Tamil Nadu. As part of this transition, the actor organised a major gathering with 3,000 women fans from districts across the state, including Salem, Cuddalore, and Kanchipuram, for official interactions and photographs. Attendees from the newly formed women's wing arrived with merchandise and presented a traditional vel, expressing firm loyalty to Dhanush and voicing ambitions to see him enter active politics and potentially contest for Chief Minister in 2031. While Dhanush has not officially declared any political ambitions, the structured event and merchandise distribution signal a coordinated expansion of his organisation.\n\n3:06\n\nThe Bharatiya Janata Party has called a nationwide demonstration following Congress President Mallikarjun Kharge's controversial remark made at an event in Patna. Kharge made the statement in response to an audience member asserting that Prime Minister Narendra Modi would not go anywhere. Denouncing the comment targeting the Prime Minister and his late father as indecent and offensive, the BJP announced demonstrations across state and district headquarters, demanding an apology from the Congress leadership.\n\nadvertisement\n\n25:35\n\nA major political row has erupted following Congress President Mallikarjun Kharge's controversial remark made during an event in Patna. In response to an audience member who stated that Prime Minister Narendra Modi would not go anywhere, Kharge retorted with remarks targeting the Prime Minister. The statement prompted sharp condemnation from Union Home Minister Amit Shah and other senior leaders of the Bharatiya Janata Party, who accused the Congress party of crossing the limits of political decency and insulting the Prime Minister's family. Meanwhile, BJP State Working Committee member Krishna Singh Kallu lodged a formal police complaint against Kharge at Patna's Kotwali Police Station. The incident triggered further confrontation over reports that the heckler was assaulted at the venue. While the Congress defended Kharge by framing the retort as colloquially used political slang and accusing the BJP of past insults against leaders like Sonia Gandhi and Rahul Gandhi, BJP representatives condemned the comment as personal abuse and an insult to constitutional decorum.","author":"India Today Television","published_date":"2022-03-09T21:15:30+05:30","latency_ms":1633.89011199979,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}